[Music]  okay everybody so this is my spoiler  review of the first eight episodes of  yellowjackets i will be doing detailed  reviews for episode nine and ten i  thought here i'll just catch you guys up  on everything i thought about the show  because i haven't been able to review it  i've been busy with other shows but i'm  so excited to jump into yellow jackets  because i've absolutely  adored this show and there's certain  reasons why i love it but it's actually  the most love coming from a place of as  a fan where  just as a fan of someone who loves tv  mysteries  this is something i've been waiting for  for a while it has that feeling of  excitement with lost where you can  call friends family members talk about  it go on reddit and you see the power of  this show is that  the amount of people on reddit for the  yellow jackets is already at like 15 000  people which is unheard of because  there's shows on tv that premiered maybe  three years ago that three seasons and  they're still only at like 6 000 people  on reddit so it's that kind of show  people want to talk about and theorize  and the strength and excitement these  kind of mysteries bring is because it's  not based off a book so it's so annoying  is a lot of tv mysteries that come out  are based off a book so you got book  readers who can just spoil the ending  and also it just kills the theory  conversation we can have on these  threads what's so great about this show  as well is that it has powerhouse  performances by its leads and shout out  juliette lewis of course i interviewed  her a year ago check that interview out  i'll link at the end of this but  yes she's amazing christina richie  amazing melanie linski amazing and i  hope i'm not butchering her name but  tawny cyprus who plays  taissa  is a show stealer here i am so impressed  by all four of them playing the roles of  the leads but that's not to undermine  how great the younger actors are and the  younger versions of these characters now  when i'm looking at it per episode base  it's not perfect and  you can tell even that feeling of the  community had where  it has such a good premiere and if you  haven't seen it you know check it out on  youtube the first episode is free it  will suck you in with that great reveal  at the end with misty and you're seeing  this image of just this lord of the  flies like area where you're like how do  we get to this and that's what makes it  so exciting is right like  what are these people now and how are  they in the past and then who are they  really we're just taking pieces together  learning more more about our characters  through the past and through the future  so you're excited to get this little  tease of where this show ends up we know  it's five seasons but  what's interesting is that  after episode one i did think it hit a  little bit of a lull where it was way  too slow and i think the lowest point  this show got to was actually episode  four which i actually did not like it's  only episode i didn't enjoy at all um  because we had  shauna on this date with adam for like  half the episode to the point like do we  need this much screen time between the  two of them how much is this serving the  plot it just felt like a lot of padding  has been put in the show the whole  season but where i think people start  getting worried was after episode four  you can even see like okay you know we  need something to happen but  you know episode five it picks up a bit  but really the other two episodes i've  loved are episode six where  we get the reveal of taissa now is  crawling eating dirt which was just  insane but also my favorite was episode  seven again based in taies's story but  with van and the wolves it was so  powerful it was intense it was kind of  that savagery we're waiting for that  brutalness and  i think episode 8 the most recent one  fell flat again which was disappointing  because i hoped it was going to keep  that momentum going it's still good but  again i feel like this shows has these  brilliant episodes of one six and seven  where the rest is okay and i hope that  in season two they can tighten it up  less padding and i think yeah obviously  people want to see as much as possible  of them when they're in the woods as  kids that's the exciting part it's  always going to be the most exciting  part i think they know that but they got  to stretch some story out it seems like  but again overall  what's standing out to me is again the  mystery aspect of this but the score is  absolutely bonkers and not just the  score right also the music selection the  songs they pick is great so you just  have a score and you have all these  great songs from the past playing mesh  together it's so good and it elevates so  much of this show now the big mystery  everyone has which gets everyone excited  about who is the antler queen i'm still  in the boat of lottie but that was a lot  based on the religious girl who just  died which shocks me by the way laura  lee that i thought laura lee was just  going to be that voice in lottie's head  encouraging her about her visions and  that this would start this kind of  crazy group that the underqueen leads i  thought that would be lottie because of  that so you know with laura lee dying  which shocked me i was actually very  interested in her character it doesn't  mean we're not going to see her in other  ways and flashbacks and stuff but i did  think she'd be a bigger part of this  puzzle especially with the religious  upbringing now i'm a huge you know if we  got teams i love jackie i hate to say it  but i do i think she's great and i find  myself siding with her a lot against  shauna and i feel like shawn has just  portrayed her horribly so yes jackie was  being insanely passive aggressive and  awful to shauna but rightfully so shauna  because she's you know sleeping with her  girls guy come on now but you know it's  just that mystery again of like are what  are we seeing on the surface and what's  going on behind it what's really the  deal with missy what's really to deal  with nat all these things blending so  well together and as a whole i think i  would give the show points wise for the  season so far i'd give it about an 8.6  and that's on the strength of those big  episodes the mystery so effective the  acting the score in particular is almost  perfect and great music selection as  well and  i think that it  has to a story like this it's gonna have  a great nine and ten i could just feel  it the final two episodes to set up the  story and it's exciting to see again a  mystery story that's planned out for  five seasons not based off a book so i'm  excited to see where this goes i'm  really pumped and i feel that energy  from this fan base so that excites me  but like i said i promise i'll be able  to do a more detailed review for episode  9 and episode 10 so please make sure to  subscribe so you don't miss those  reviews and please follow me at steve  all the show on twitter instagram and  tick tock for more of me  and i'll see you next time

